    cor:studyCollectionMarkRaw "This coin is boxed in the Study Collection as Nicomedia" ;
    cor:attributionNoteRaw "All depends on how one reads the third letter. N is possible and this coin is boxed in the Study Collection as Nicomedia, cf. RIC 7.633, 191 (330-335). However, H is also possible for Heraclea (RIC 7.557, 113A), 330-333. The bust is draped and cuirassed, not just cuirassed, which ought to favor Heraclea. The N's on the obverse are more obviously diagonal; legend and officina work for either." ;
